    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello. I'm Dr. Smith. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S032",
      "patient_response": "Well, Dr. Smith, I... I guess I'm here because things have just gotten so dark lately, you know? Like, really dark. I wake up—when I actually can sleep, which isn't often—and my first thought is just, 'Why did I wake up?' It just feels like it would be so much better, so much easier for everyone, if I just... didn't. If I just went to sleep and that was it. And it's not just a passing thought, it's like this heavy blanket over me all day while I'm trying to work. I lay carpet and tile, you know, and it's hard work, on your knees all day, and lately, I just stare at the floor and think about how dying would just be... fair. Like a fair punishment. Because I've just ruined everything. I've let my family down, I've messed things up with my crew at work... I just feel like I'm a burden, and maybe if I was gone, they wouldn't have to deal with me anymore. I just can't shake this feeling that I deserve to die for all the mistakes I've made, and it just plays over and over in my head.",
