    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever felt this way for a period of at least two weeks at any point in your life before this current stretch?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "I... I don't really know. I mean, I guess it's possible? It's just so hard to remember what things were like before this, you know? Like, when you're in the middle of it, when it's this heavy, it feels like it's always been this way. I try to think back to, like, a year ago, or five years ago, and it's all just a blur of laying tile, driving to the next job, coming home... I know there were times I felt down, sure. Everyone feels down sometimes, especially when the work dries up or when my knees are just screaming at me after a twelve-hour day on the floor. But this... this feeling of just wanting to disappear, of feeling like I *should* disappear because I'm so worthless... I don't know if I've ever felt it this strongly, or for this long, before right now. Or maybe I did and I just pushed it down? I used to be so good at just putting my head down and working through things. You know, just spread the mortar, lay the tile, make sure the lines are straight, and don't think about anything else. But now I can't even do that. The thoughts just bleed into everything. So, to answer your question... I honestly couldn't tell you if it's ever been exactly two weeks like this before. It just feels like forever right now.",
